jxl-c NOTICE
============

This repository is a single C library that combines JPEG XL decode and encode
code from more than one upstream project. Treat file headers and the licenses
listed below as authoritative for each source file.

Decode pipeline (jxl-oxide port)
--------------------------------
Much of the decode path under `src/` (outside `src/encoder/`) and the matching
public decode headers are a manual C port of jxl-oxide:

  https://github.com/tirr-c/jxl-oxide

Those files are dual-licensed under MIT and Apache 2.0. See:

  LICENSE-MIT
  LICENSE-APACHE

Encoder / CMS (JPEG XL Project / libjxl)
----------------------------------------
The JPEG→JXL encoder, CMS helpers, and related public headers adapted from
libjxl live primarily under `src/encoder/` and in public headers such as
`include/jxl/encode.h`, `include/jxl/cms.h`, `include/jxl/cms_interface.h`,
`include/jxl/color_encoding.h`, and `include/jxl/codestream_header.h`.

Those files are BSD-licensed (JPEG XL Project Authors). See:

  LICENSE-BSD
  src/encoder/LICENSE-BSD   (same text, kept next to encoder sources)
  src/encoder/PATENTS

Simple lossless
---------------
`include/jxl/simple_lossless.h` and `src/encoder/simple_lossless.c` carry
MIT OR Apache-2.0 SPDX markers and also note availability under the encoder
BSD terms / patent grant where applicable. Prefer the SPDX marker on the file.

Third-party dependencies
------------------------
Brotli, LCMS2, and other vendored or system dependencies keep their own
licenses as shipped by those projects.
